{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>A man oppressed with blood</b> — like עושק, and so אגור like אוגר השדודה, like השודדה השכוני, like השוכן. And one who is עושק בדם נפש, a murderer — his sins will bring him into trouble, that he go to the pit to kill his soul and cast it in an evil place, and none will be found to restore him. Another interpretation: a man oppressed in his property and in himself on account of blood of a life that he shed, until his descent to the pit — he will flee from place to place, for he fears for his life, and the pit is an allusion to the grave." "<b>Let them not support him</b> — by way of warning, meaning that others should not support him when he falls nor have pity on him, because he destroyed the one formed in the image of Elohim."], :book :proverbs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {0 "The chain of comparison אגור/אוגר/שדודה/שכוני/שוכן is rendered verbatim as Ibn Ezra quotes or reconstructs each related Hebrew form; the textual integrity of the chain is uncertain but translated literally without emendation."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Proverbs -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/mishley/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:25:16.185934653Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}